WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.236 --> 00:00:19.150
It was early on a Thursday morning when Sherlock Holmes made up his mind.

2
00:00:19.151 --> 00:00:24.412
"Watson," he said to me over breakfast, "I have decided that I really must go after all."

3
00:00:24.413 --> 00:00:26.571
"Go! Where to?"

4
00:00:26.572 --> 00:00:33.301
"To Dartmoor to investigate the disappearance of Silver Blaze, the racehorse, and the murder of his trainer, John Straker."

5
00:00:33.302 --> 00:00:38.975
I was not surprised by Holmes' decision; in fact, I wondered why he hadn't gone sooner.

6
00:00:38.976 --> 00:00:45.551
For the past two days the great detective had been poring over the newspapers, which were filled with stories about the case.

7
00:00:45.552 --> 00:00:51.384
Silver Blaze, named for a white patch on his forehead, had been favored to win the Wessex Cup race.

8
00:00:51.385 --> 00:00:54.951
"I would be happy to go with you if I wouldn't be in the way," I said.

9
00:00:54.952 --> 00:01:00.943
"My dear Watson, you could help me a great deal by coming along and bringing your excellent binoculars.

10
00:01:00.944 --> 00:01:05.788
If we hurry, we just have time to catch our train at Paddington Station."

11
00:01:05.789 --> 00:01:11.851
And so I soon found myself sitting on a train speeding toward Dartmoor while Holmes read the latest newspapers.

12
00:01:11.852 --> 00:01:15.782
When he thrust the last one under the seat, he was ready to talk.

13
00:01:15.783 --> 00:01:24.020
"On Tuesday night I received telegrams from Colonel Ross, the horse's owner, and Inspector Gregory, who is in charge of the investigation," said Holmes.

14
00:01:24.021 --> 00:01:26.365
"They wanted my help with the case."

15
00:01:26.366 --> 00:01:30.277
"Tuesday night! Why didn't you go to Dartmoor yesterday?"

16
00:01:30.278 --> 00:01:35.835
"Because I made a mistake, which I do more often than people realize," admitted the great detective.

17
00:01:35.836 --> 00:01:42.423
"I thought it would be difficult to hide England's most famous racehorse, especially in such a sparsely inhabited place.

18
00:01:42.424 --> 00:01:48.157
At any moment I expected to hear that Silver Blaze had been found and that his abductor was the murderer.

19
00:01:48.158 --> 00:01:53.585
But all that has happened is that a young man named Fitzroy Simpson has been arrested."

20
00:01:53.586 --> 00:01:58.557
Although I had read some newspaper stories, Holmes wanted to go over the facts again with me.

21
00:01:58.558 --> 00:02:03.303
"Nothing clears up a case faster than describing it to another person," he explained.

22
00:02:03.304 --> 00:02:07.733
So I sat back while he gave me a summary of the events that had led to our journey.

23
00:02:07.734 --> 00:02:15.241
"Every precaution was taken to guard Silver Blaze at Colonel Ross' stable, which housed only four horses," said Holmes.

24
00:02:15.242 --> 00:02:20.978
"Straker had worked for the colonel for a dozen years, first as a jockey and then as a trainer.

25
00:02:20.979 --> 00:02:24.970
He had always shown himself to be an honest and hard-working employee."

26
00:02:24.971 --> 00:02:30.871
The trainer and his wife lived with a maid in a small, red-brick house about two hundred yards from the stable.

27
00:02:30.872 --> 00:02:38.369
Besides Straker, there were three young grooms who worked with the horses. All three were trustworthy boys.

28
00:02:38.370 --> 00:02:42.953
One groom stayed up each night in the stable while the other two slept in the loft.

29
00:02:42.954 --> 00:02:50.445
The country around the stable was very lonely. About half a mile north was a cluster of houses, where travelers often stayed.

30
00:02:50.446 --> 00:02:59.189
The town of Tavistock lay two miles away to the west. Across the moor and also about two miles away was Mapleton, a larger training stable.

31
00:02:59.190 --> 00:03:08.357
Lord Brackwater owned this stable, and Silas Brown was the manager. Otherwise the moor was a complete wilderness, inhabited only by a few Gypsies.

32
00:03:08.358 --> 00:03:12.087
On Monday night Colonel Ross' stable was locked at nine o'clock.

33
00:03:12.088 --> 00:03:17.765
Two grooms went to Straker's house for supper while the third, Ned Hunter, remained on guard in the stable.

34
00:03:17.766 --> 00:03:24.750
The maid, Edith Baxter, was bringing him a supper of curried lamb when a young man suddenly appeared out of the darkness.

35
00:03:24.751 --> 00:03:30.592
He looked like a gentleman, dressed in a gray tweed suit with a red-and-black scarf and a cloth cap.

36
00:03:30.593 --> 00:03:35.172
She noticed that he was carrying a heavy walking stick with a large knob on top.

37
00:03:35.173 --> 00:03:44.148
"Stop, miss!" he called. "Can you tell me where I am? I had almost made up my mind to sleep on the moor when I saw the light of your lantern."

38
00:03:44.149 --> 00:03:47.648
"You are at Colonel Ross' stable," replied Edith.

39
00:03:47.649 --> 00:03:55.637
"What luck!" said the man. "I understand that a groom is on guard there every night. Perhaps that is his supper you are carrying."

40
00:03:55.638 --> 00:03:59.645
The man reached into his pocket and pulled out a folded piece of white paper.

41
00:03:59.646 --> 00:04:03.967
"See that the boy gets this, and I'll give you enough money to buy a new dress."

42
00:04:03.968 --> 00:04:10.055
The maid was afraid of the man and ran past him to the window, where she always handed in the meals.

43
00:04:10.056 --> 00:04:14.278
It was already open and Hunter was seated at a table inside the stable.

44
00:04:14.279 --> 00:04:18.302
She began to tell him what had happened when the stranger approached the window.

45
00:04:18.303 --> 00:04:22.534
"Good evening," he said to Hunter. "I want to have a word with you."

46
00:04:22.535 --> 00:04:25.700
"What business do you have here?" asked the boy.

47
00:04:25.701 --> 00:04:34.864
"It's business that could put money in your pocket. You have a horse running in the Wessex Cup race—Silver Blaze. What can you tell me about his chances?"

48
00:04:34.865 --> 00:04:40.276
"I won't give you any information," said Hunter. "Leave this property at once!"

49
00:04:40.277 --> 00:04:46.272
The groom quickly untied the dog and went out to chase the man away. But the man had disappeared.

50
00:04:46.273 --> 00:04:53.513
"One moment," I said, interrupting Holmes' story. "When the groom ran outside, did he leave the stable door unlocked?"

51
00:04:53.514 --> 00:04:58.767
"An excellent question, Watson. But no, he locked it."

52
00:04:58.768 --> 00:05:02.925
Hunter waited to tell Straker until the other grooms had returned from supper.

53
00:05:02.926 --> 00:05:08.933
Straker was upset by the story and around one o'clock in the morning Mrs. Straker awoke to find him dressing.

54
00:05:08.934 --> 00:05:14.840
He said that he was going out to check on Silver Blaze. She begged him not to go because it was raining.

55
00:05:14.841 --> 00:05:19.490
At seven o'clock, Mrs. Straker awoke and noticed that her husband had not returned.

56
00:05:19.491 --> 00:05:26.905
She and the maid set off for the stables where they found Hunter in some kind of stupor, Silver Blaze's stall empty, and no sign of her husband.

57
00:05:26.906 --> 00:05:32.318
The dog was asleep in its corner. Mrs. Straker quickly woke the two other grooms in the loft.

58
00:05:32.319 --> 00:05:36.135
They had heard nothing during the night because they were both sound sleepers.

59
00:05:36.136 --> 00:05:41.895
Hunter was obviously under the influence of some powerful drug, so he was left at the stable to recover.

60
00:05:41.896 --> 00:05:46.816
The two women and the two grooms ran out in search of Straker and the horse.

61
00:05:46.817 --> 00:05:51.476
About a quarter mile from the stable, Straker's coat was flapping from a bush.

62
00:05:51.477 --> 00:05:57.802
His dead body was nearby; he had been hit on the head with a heavy instrument and had a long cut on his thigh.

63
00:05:57.803 --> 00:06:02.043
Apparently he had tried to fight back because he had a small knife in his right hand.

64
00:06:02.044 --> 00:06:07.361
In his left hand he had the red-and-black scarf that the maid recognized as belonging to the stranger.

65
00:06:07.362 --> 00:06:12.196
From the hoofprints in the mud, it was easy to see that Silver Blaze had been there too.

66
00:06:12.197 --> 00:06:17.442
"Hunter was certain that the stranger had put something in his food while it was at the window," said Holmes.

67
00:06:17.443 --> 00:06:25.763
"And indeed the food remaining on his plate was found to contain a large quantity of powdered opium. Everyone else who ate the curry was fine."

68
00:06:25.764 --> 00:06:28.692
"But what happened to the horse?" I asked.

69
00:06:28.693 --> 00:06:37.005
"Although Colonel Ross has offered a large reward," said Holmes, "Silver Blaze has not been seen since that night."
